      "id": 1,
      "text": "In 1828, a Mexican rancher named Antonio Chaboya discovered a natural mineral spring in Alum Rock, sparking its early fame.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.sanjoseca.gov/Home/Components/News/News/5526/4765"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Alum Rock once thrived as a grand resort in the late 1800s, drawing visitors for its reputed healing waters.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://roamingverse.com/explore/united-states/california/alum-rock"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Alum Rock Village boasts local culinary staples like fresh tamales from The Tamale Factory and burnt almond cake from Peter’s Bakery.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.sanjoseca.gov/Home/Components/News/News/5526/4765"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Roberto Cruz Alum Rock Branch Library serves as a hub for community engagement and education in the neighborhood.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.sanjoseca.gov/Home/Components/News/News/5526/4765"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Hike or bike along scenic trails that wind through rolling hills, uncover unique mineral springs, and admire Penitencia Creek in Alum Rock Park.",
